  "graph": {
    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Gamepad Jam: drums and chords played from a game controller. Press Space and a demo plays the same parts, so the patch makes sound before a controller is plugged in.\n\nConnect a controller (the Devices tab lists it), press its Start button to play, and press Select (back), or click the Controller switch, to take over from the demo. A, B, X, and Y play the kick, snare, closed hat, and open hat. D-pad right strums the next chord (Am, F, C, G) and D-pad left starts the progression over. The left stick sweeps the filter and the right stick its resonance; pull the right trigger to strum harder and the left trigger for echo. Ctrl+Tab shows the Jam panel."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            -330.0
          ],
          "size": [
            760.0,
            168.0
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "kind": "gamepad",
        "config": {
          "pad": 1
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            0.0
          ],
          "label": "Gamepad"
        },
        "hide_unwired": true
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "The Gamepad node turns the controller into signals: every button has a gate and a _press trigger, and the sticks and triggers are numbers. Only its wired sockets show here (Hide Unwired Sockets, Ctrl+H, shows them all again).\n\nThe sticks and triggers reach the patch another way: they are bound to inputs, the way right-click ▸ Bind… binds any unwired input to a control, and so are Start (play/stop) and Select (the Controller switch). The Project tab lists every binding. The Devices tab's Add gamepad transport buttons puts play/stop on A, which here is the kick, so this jam binds Start instead."
        },
        "ui": {
          "pos": [
            0.0,
            200.0
          ],
          "size": [
            466.0,
            216.0
          ]
        }
      },
