      {
        "id": "1c",
        "kind": "comment",
        "config": {
          "text": "Chord step counts the steps, 0 to 3, and Chord root turns the count into a root note: A, F, C, then G (0 is G, so the first step lands on A). Strum, a Note To MIDI, plays the root for 1.8 s on every step; Triad builds a major chord on it, and In A minor snaps that into the key, so A becomes A minor while F, C, and G stay major. Strings plucks a Karplus-Strong String for every note, and the Filter follows the Cutoff and Resonance knobs, which the sticks move."
        },
        "ui": {
